    "titulo": "Home, renting and neighbours",
    "objetivo": "Name the rooms and the floors of a home, talk about renting a flat and its costs, and politely raise a small problem with a neighbour or a landlord. Use «a» for a floor («al terzo piano»), «da» for what a room is for («la camera da letto»), «servire» in the plural, and the polite «Potrebbe…?». Avoid the English-speaker traps: «di» for the purpose of a room, «per» after «cercare» and «essere» for being right.",
